From 43be33f73e46391e9bddfd9bc3671173dd844753 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ivarne-agent <ivar.nesje+agent@digdir.no>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:29:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(studioctl): localtest-v2 runtime with the platform's own
 services

Adds `studioctl env up -r localtest-v2`, which runs the production Register,
Authentication, PDP, Access Management, Storage and Events (built by the
localtest-research repository) with a localtest app for the test-user login
and token helpers, a shared Postgres, and the same PDF generator and workflow
engine as the localtest runtime.

studioctl-server is the front door while it runs: it listens on the public
origin, forwards each platform prefix to the component's loopback port and
/{org}/{app} to the discovered app, and deploys each app to the platform
(metadata and texts to Storage, the policy to the PDP, test users to the
Register) before reporting it ready. Apps keep binding to loopback; there is
no host bridge in this mode. The components reach the public origin through
the container runtime's host gateway.

The images are pinned to one build; `--latest` follows main,
STUDIOCTL_LOCALTEST_V2_TAG names a build, and `--dev <component>` builds one
from a research checkout. Readiness is an HTTP poll of every component's
health endpoint. Only one runtime runs at a time, and the other env commands
act on the one `env up` last started.
